1
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:17,000
Seventeen-year-old Tom Davidson hasn’t left his home since he was 15.

2
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:21,142
The last time he went out was two years ago.

3
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:27,960
He was walking to catch a bus when he was hit on the head by a sign falling from a building.

4
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:35,460
He spent more than two months in hospital and doctors told him he was lucky to be alive.

5
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:44,180
The accident left Tom with agoraphobia: the idea of being outdoors makes him feel extremely anxious.

6
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:48,560
The problem is that Tom loves travelling.

7
00:00:49,380 --> 00:01:02,400
Before his accident, Tom spent most weekends exploring his home city of London by bus, underground train and his scooter, and he looked forward to holidays abroad with his parents.

8
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:10,113
Now the idea of driving in a car to France or taking a plane to Italy terrifies him.

9
00:01:10,693 --> 00:01:22,060
However, there is a way that Tom can still visit the most remote corners of the world without leaving the security of his home: Google Maps.

10
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:31,540
In the last year and a half, Tom has visited every country in the world where Google Maps has been and taken photos.

11
00:01:32,580 --> 00:01:50,434
Using ‘street view’, he has walked down the streets of the world’s most famous cities, he has seen all the world’s most amazing geographical features and he has visited places in the world that he didn’t know existed: all of this from the comfort of his home.

12
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:57,600
Tom’s virtual travel is more than just a hobby – it has become an art project.

13
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:12,060
He has taken more than 5,000 screenshots of places he has visited and last week, there was an exhibition of his best photos at a school near his home (but of course, he didn’t go).

14
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:19,340
Tom also hopes that his online journeys will help him eventually to overcome his agoraphobia.

15
00:02:20,170 --> 00:02:28,631
As he discovers more places that he wants to visit one day, he is becoming more and more determined to leave his home.

16
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:37,460
And his dream, if he can, is to work in the travel industry, for example as a flight attendant or a tour guide.
